  "Question": "Jamie counted the number of edges of a cube, Jimmy counted the number of corners, and Judy counted the number of faces. They then added the three numbers. What was the resulting sum?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(16\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(22\\)",
    "E": "\\(26\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Count the cube in groups so that nothing is counted twice. There are \\(4\\) edges around the top, \\(4\\) around the bottom, and \\(4\\) joining them, for \\(12\\) edges. There are \\(4\\) top corners and \\(4\\) bottom corners, for \\(8\\) corners. The faces are the top, the bottom, and the \\(4\\) sides, for \\(6\\) faces.\n\nTheir sum is\n\\[\n12+8+6=\\boxed{26},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
